Jihad: pinch/fit ZOOM + visual-viewport pan in the offscreen render.

PuppetWidget::JihadRenderDocument (added by 0005, caret by 0011) rendered a
fixed (0,0,w,h) CSS-px rect at scale 1, so the daemon's SetResolution/SetFullZoom
never magnified the RenderDocument capture — they only relocated content into a
1/zoom quadrant ("zoom is poor / things get cut off"). This adds real zoom:

  - JihadRenderDocument takes (aZoom, aPanX, aPanY). When |Z-1| > 1% (or panned)
    it pre-scales the gfxContext by Z and renders an ABSOLUTE DOCUMENT rect
    (RENDER_IGNORE_VIEWPORT_SCROLLING | RENDER_DOCUMENT_RELATIVE), so w/Z x h/Z
    CSS px fill the w x h device buffer at Zx and the whole page is reachable in
    both axes (no display-list culling, no engine-scroll dependence). A near-1
    fit-zoom stays viewport-relative so window.onscroll/fixed/sticky keep working.
  - The C entry point is renamed jihad_offscreen_render_document_v2 (5 args) so a
    stale daemon/libxul mismatch fails loudly at RTLD_NOW load (extern C has no
    parameter mangling). See render/goanna/{GoannaRenderPage,BrowserPageGoanna}.

Layout viewport is left at the window width (no reflow) so this can't re-arm the
landscape fit-zoom feedback loop. See context/impl/zoom-fix-2026-07-27.md.

